  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthened institutional capacity of employers&apos; organizations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Since 2013, the ILO&apos;s efforts have significantly enhanced the Federation of Egyptian Industries (FEI), Egypt&apos;s leading employer organization representing over 104,000 industrial enterprises (90%+ private sector), over 2 million workers, and 18% of the national economy. The FEI has bolstered its presence, becoming a more prominent voice for businesses. It has established three new ILO-supported units, expanded regionally beyond Cairo, and introduced new services. The FEI leadership is committed to advancing both economic and social agendas.
In the previous two years, with funding from Finland, the Netherlands, Norway, the US, the UK, and Sweden, the ILO supported FEI to boost its visibility and social agenda. This involved technical assistance in human resources, gender, and refugee/host community integration. The ILO also helped FEI develop new training content and advisory services on issues like child labor, employer-led childcare, human trafficking, freedom of association, corporate social responsibility, and enterprise formalization.
This biennium, a Rapid Situational Analysis (RSA) on Just Transition, focusing on Women&apos;s Entrepreneurship Development in Egypt, aimed to gather targeted information on opportunities for women entrepreneurs. Following prior work on enterprise formalization, the ILO will support the development of a new training service on enterprise formalization. Additionally, the ILO will back two more cycles of the FEI Human Resources and Gender Academy and continue to provide capacity development to FEI on the application and implications of the new trade union law for companies.</narrative>
  </description>
